1. Source-available, not open source

The Enterprise Code is published in source form so that it can be reviewed,
built and deployed together with the rest of maverickbuilds.app.

2. Without a subscription: Enterprise Features switched off

You may read and copy the Enterprise Code, build it together with the rest of
maverickbuilds.app, and install and run the result, including the images the
licensor publishes, which contain it, for any use the Sustainable Use License
permits, as long as the Enterprise Features stay switched off. Running the
Enterprise Code that this involves is permitted.

You may share unmodified copies of the Enterprise Code as part of a complete
copy of the repository shared under the Sustainable Use License, with this
license and every notice intact.

3. With a subscription: Enterprise Features switched on

Subject to a valid, unexpired license key issued by the licensor for an
agreement you have accepted with it (a "Subscription"), the licensor grants
you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to use the
Enterprise Features for the term, edition and scope that agreement states. A
license key implements the agreement; it grants no right the agreement does
not.

4. Limitations

Except as a Subscription or another written agreement with the licensor
allows, you may not:

- switch on or use Enterprise Features, or change the software so that it
  treats them as licensed;
- create, alter or use license keys the licensor did not issue, or remove,
  disable or circumvent the license-key checks;
- distribute modified Enterprise Code, or distribute, sublicense, resell, host
  for third parties or otherwise make the Enterprise Code available beyond
  section 2;
- alter, remove, or obscure any licensing, copyright, or other notices of the
  licensor.

5. Term and termination

Your rights under section 3 end when your Subscription expires or terminates,
as its agreement provides. You may then go on using the rest of
maverickbuilds.app under the Sustainable Use License, with the Enterprise
Features switched off as section 2 describes.

If you breach these terms, your license ends automatically.

